{"data":{"status":true,"competition":{"id":1764222,"visibility":"public","theme_colour":"light-blue_un","paid":0,"title":"CodeBreaker","festival_id":null,"organization_id":561,"web_url":null,"start_date":"2026-10-01T00:00:00+05:30","end_date":"2026-10-25T17:18:00+05:30","location":null,"type":"hackathons","public_url":"hackathons\/codebreaker-inderprastha-engineering-college-ipec-ghaziabad-1764222","region":"online","details":"<p><strong>Overview:<\/strong><\/p>\n<p><strong>CodeBreaker<\/strong> is an online hackathon conducted by <strong>Kira&rsquo;s Logic &times; CodeBlooded<\/strong>, designed to challenge participants to think creatively, solve real-world problems, and turn their ideas into working prototypes.<\/p>\n<p><strong>Hackathon Format:<\/strong><\/p>\n<p>The hackathon will be conducted in <strong>3 rounds<\/strong>:<\/p>\n<p><strong>Round 1 &mdash; Idea\/PPT Submission:<\/strong><\/p>\n<p>Participants will submit their solution idea in the prescribed PPT format. Submissions will be evaluated based on problem understanding, innovation, feasibility, proposed solution, and overall presentation.<\/p>\n<p><strong>Round 2 &mdash; Online Mentorship &amp; Refinement:<\/strong><\/p>\n<p>Shortlisted teams will receive <strong>online mentorship<\/strong> to refine their ideas, improve their technical approach, and develop their prototype. Mentors may provide guidance on technology, implementation, scalability, and presentation.<\/p>\n<p><strong>Round 3 &mdash; Grand Finale: Prototype Demonstration:<\/strong><\/p>\n<p>Finalist teams will present and demonstrate their <strong>working prototype online<\/strong> before the judging panel. Teams will explain their solution, demonstrate its functionality, and answer questions from the judges.<\/p>\n<p><strong>Eligibility:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Open to students and aspiring developers\/innovators.<\/li>\n<li>Participants may register individually or as a team.<\/li>\n<li>Inter-college teams are allowed.<\/li>\n<li>Participants from different academic specializations are allowed.<\/li>\n<li>Teams should follow the maximum team-size requirement specified during registration.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Rules:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>All submissions must be the original work of the participating team.<\/li>\n<li>Teams must submit their work within the announced deadlines.<\/li>\n<li>Participants may use open-source technologies, APIs, frameworks, and publicly available resources, while complying with their respective licenses.<\/li>\n<li>Plagiarism or submission of substantially copied projects may result in disqualification.<\/li>\n<li>Teams must be available for the online mentorship and Grand Finale rounds if shortlisted.<\/li>\n<li>The prototype demonstrated in the Grand Finale should correspond to the solution submitted during the hackathon.<\/li>\n<li>Judges' decisions regarding qualification and evaluation will be final.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Evaluation Criteria:<\/strong><\/p>\n<p>Projects may be evaluated on:<\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Innovation &amp; Creativity<\/li>\n<li>Problem Understanding<\/li>\n<li>Technical Implementation<\/li>\n<li>Feasibility &amp; Scalability<\/li>\n<li>Prototype Functionality<\/li>\n<li>Impact &amp; Usefulness<\/li>\n<li>Presentation &amp; Demonstration<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Mode:<\/strong><\/p>\n<p>The entire hackathon will be conducted <strong>online<\/strong>, including submissions, mentorship sessions, and the Grand Finale prototype demonstration.<\/p>\n<p><strong>Build your idea. Break the problem. Create the solution.<\/strong><\/p>\n<p><strong>CodeBreaker &mdash; Kira&rsquo;s Logic &times; CodeBlooded<\/strong><\/p>\n<p><strong>Join whatsapp group:<\/strong> <a href=\"https:\/\/chat.whatsapp.com\/C31p5m651XS7Hataktndjr\">https:\/\/chat.whatsapp.com\/C31p5m651XS7Hataktndjr<\/a><\/p>","overall_prizes":"Exciting prizes, certificates, recognition, and opportunities for winning teams and participants.","regn_open":1,"regn_type":1,"regn_url":nul